FILE: coverage.rs
MOD: commands/coverage
OWNS: unmapped source file detection — walks filesystem against declared module ownership
PROFILE: [io, pure-core]
CHANGE-FREQUENCY: stable

CoverageResult: record — unmapped: Vec<String>

check: &ArchContext → Result<CoverageResult, String> [io]
  calls: context::walk_module_files, schema::is_directory_owner, is_in_covered_dir
  called-by: run, stale::run

run: bool → Result<(), String> [io, boundary]
  calls: ArchContext::load, check

is_in_covered_dir: &Path * &HashSet<PathBuf> → bool [pure]
  note: walks ancestor dirs upward — a file is covered if any ancestor is a covered_dirs entry

DEPENDS-ON: context, schema

KEY-INVARIANTS:
- Directory-owner modules (entry-point files like mod.rs, __init__.py) cover their entire subtree — is_in_covered_dir must climb all ancestors, not just the immediate parent
- coverage uses COVERAGE_EXTENSIONS (broader set) not SOURCE_EXTENSIONS — a file can be covered by drift but not coverage if its extension is in SOURCE but not COVERAGE

